=== SURVEY (web source of truth, read end-to-end) ===
web/src/features/dashboard/widgets/VersionInfoWidget.tsx:
  Data: useVersionInfo() (GET /system/version) drives loading/error/hasData (web
        `hasData = version.data != null`); useCaptureStats() (GET /dev-tools/telemetry-capture/stats)
        feeds the stat grid. Both read defensively (versionData/captureData as loose records).
  Breakpoints: isCompact = size.cols <= 1 ; isWide = size.cols >= 4.
  Compose: WidgetShell chrome (title hidden when compact, freshness indicator, refresh);
           compact = version (bold) + neutral Badge(truncatedSha);
           standard = KVList[Version(bold), Build Date, Git SHA(mono), Go Version, Uptime]
                      + WidgetStatGrid[Signals/sec, Messages Today] cols=2;
           wide = + "OS: … • Arch: …" line + WidgetStatGrid adds [Bytes Processed, Avg Latency] cols=4;
           empty (no version data) = EmptyState "No version data available".
  Helpers: truncatedSha = gitSha?.slice(0,7) ?? '—'; field fallbacks `?? '—'`; stat fallbacks `?? 0`;
           local formatBytes: <1KiB "{int} B", <1MiB "{1dp} KB", <1GiB "{1dp} MB", else "{2dp} GB"
           (note GB uses TWO decimals); signalsPerSec = fmtNumber(_,1); messagesToday = fmtInt;
           avgLatency = `${fmtNumber(_,1)} ms`.
Registry (web/src/features/dashboard/widgets/registry/system.ts → "version-info"): category system,
  default 2×2, min 1×2, max 4×40.

